    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Is the explainer giving source-backed suggestions for measured slow interactions?\nChrome measures the live [react-inp-blame demo](https://reactinpblame.com), then the AI SDK explains its report. This is a demo workload. Each finished answer is checked for a successful source response, the exact blamed name, a source citation and a recommended strategy ID matching a documented demo option. The strategy check does not validate the prose or establish that a change works. Suggestions have not been applied or benchmarked. Source files are the pinned ea73e5d snapshot, not a verified copy of the current deploy. Summary: rolling last hour; activity detail: last six hours; freshness: last completed response, stale after 20 minutes. The pretend-shop agent is in dashboard/reference.json."
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "vector(1)",
          "legendFormat": "__auto",
          "refId": "A",
          "range": false,
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "transparent": true,
      "id": 1,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 4
      }
    },
